pe="html">Fighting has returned to northern Ethiopia, shattering a fragile peace in the region. DW spoke to civilians caught in the crossfire amid communication blackouts, as rebel and federal forces keep battling for territory.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>TV journalist is crowned king of Uganda's Tooro Kingdom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4ba0691bd509f11f1e2d61dc0e1f4717ceb062a517686c41361ce69ca0fa2e6</id><updated>2026-09-29T20:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tv-journalist-is-crowned-king-of-uganda-s-tooro-kingdom/a-79475911--6e0b4c2080aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tv-journalist-is-crowned-king-of-uganda-s-tooro-kingdom/a-79475911?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Edward Rukidi Kijanangoma has ascended to the throne after King Oyo died at the age of 34 due to a cancer battle. He previously worked for Ugandan broadcaster UBC as a TV anchor and editor.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Senegal's Youth Olympics makes Olympics in Africa 'logical'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:169984085d644b89ea72d29c527dc0b42f092b0b5ec517d9d68894c908f078f5</id><updated>2026-09-29T20:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975--7dbe2801c775.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/senegal-s-youth-olympics-makes-olympics-in-africa-logical/a-79468975?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Youth Olympics are to be hosted in Africa for the first time ever. The edition in Senegal is also a chance to prove the continent can host a full Olympics in the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa: Is murder on the rise again?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d8b9481782ace797e6e693e5f9a709a1a4c57d689a75e76867f39663833d86a</id><updated>2026-09-29T20:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-is-murder-on-the-rise-again/a-79462242--cb357388c9bd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-is-murder-on-the-rise-again/a-79462242?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Africa has one of the world's highest murder rates, though the latest figures show that murders are falling. So why does violence still feel so pervasive — and what will it take to overcome this spiral of violence?</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry></feed>
